## 2. Using strace with `-T` and parsing with awk

```bash
# Get timing for each syscall and count them
strace -T -f -e trace=all command 2>&1 | \
  awk '/^[^ \t]+\(0x[0-9a-f]+\): [0-9]+.[0-9]+ = [0-9]+$/ { 
    syscall = $1; 
    time = $2; 
    count[syscall]++; 
    total[syscall] += time; 
  } 
  END { 
    printf "%-50s %10s %10s\n", "SYSCALL", "COUNT", "TIME"; 
    printf "%-50s %10s %10s\n", "--------------------------", "----------", "----------"; 
    for (s in count) { 
      printf "%-50s %10d %10.3f\n", s, count[s], total[s]; 
    } 
  }'
```

